  "sport": "soccer",
  "title": "Three goals – score, then defend",
  "description": "Three small goals stand in a line, with a marked shooting zone in front of them. Two teams line up a little way off, everyone with a ball. The first red player dribbles towards any goal, gets into the shooting zone and passes the ball in. Then they run round the goal and become a defender.\n\nThe moment the ball goes in, the first blue player sets off towards any goal. When blue has scored, the next red player goes, and blue runs round their goal and defends. Goals far apart make it easier for the attacker, goals close together make it harder.\n\nProgressions: just touch the goal instead of running round it, or defend straight away. If the defender wins the ball, play 1 v 1. Hardest: shoot from anywhere – but if you miss, you must run round the goal before you can defend.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Look up while you dribble – which goal is open?"
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Change direction and pace to get past the defender."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Pass the ball in with the inside of the foot – safe, not hard."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "After scoring: turn quickly and defend straight away."
    }
  ],
